# Model and media files must never be line-ending normalised.
#
# There is a real trap here: Kenney ships ASCII FBX with CRLF terminators, so
# Git's auto-detection classifies them as text and offers to rewrite every line.
# KayKit ships binary FBX. Marking the whole family binary keeps both intact and
# keeps diffs out of the log.
*.fbx   binary
*.FBX   binary
*.obj   binary
*.blend binary
*.dae   binary
*.glb   binary
*.gltf  binary
*.stl   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.tga   binary
*.psd   binary
*.exr   binary
*.hdr   binary
*.ogg   binary
*.wav   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.bundle filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.so filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
